1
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:05,140
Enhance Armament!

2
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,470
Oh, my God.

3
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:03,140
Kirito, Kirito, say something, Kirito!

4
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,120
Let's go!

5
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,317
Thank

6
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,717
you

7
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:47,800
so

8
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:03,057
much for watching.

9
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:06,937
I'd like to see the way I'm learning.

10
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:12,720
I'm going to connect
you to the way you buy.

11
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:16,900
You're the way I hear you.

12
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:24,217
I'm going to the same way you can't.

13
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,060
I'm going to go myself.

14
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,100
Oh...

15
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,060
Kirito!

16
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,720
Come on, wake up!

17
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,577
System call.

18
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,440
Generate luminous element.

19
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:58,637
System call.

20
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,040
Transfer human unit durability.

21
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,620
Self to lift.

22
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:08,860
Don't die.

23
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:11,960
That's enough, Eugeo.

24
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,180
I think I'll be okay now.

25
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,380
Whoa, take it easy.

26
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,151
You were hurt pretty bad.

27
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:21,617
You might have internal wounds
my healing didn't catch.

28
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:24,700
It's not as bad as when
those goblins beat me down.

29
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:28,300
Anyway, I'm worried about her. What?

30
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,260
Who cares?

31
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,462
She tried to kill you, remember?

32
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:38,160
I know what you said before, about
letting hate get the better of me.

33
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,480
She was just doing her duty.

34
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:44,114
She wasn't fighting for revenge
or because she hated us.

35
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:45,260
I get that.

36
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:48,600
Still, that's no excuse.

37
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:51,937
I can't forgive the church
or the Integrity Knights.

38
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:55,637
They have all this power, but
they're just a bunch of hypocrites.

39
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:59,060
If they really wanted to
protect humanity, they could.

40
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,680
They'd rather protect a lie instead.

41
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:07,375
I know what you mean, but you can't
forget these knights are human, too.

42
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:11,759
They got their own problems, like
how this one felt about her gender.

43
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:17,720
I gotta say, your perfect
weapon control art's awesome.

44
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:20,885
Those knights didn't
stand a chance against it.

45
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,840
This fight's over.

46
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:27,396
There's no reason to hate Fanatio
and the Four Whirling Blades anymore.

47
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,560
So let it go.

48
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:31,380
They're human.

49
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,680
Yeah, you're right.

50
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:37,241
I understood that much
about her during the fight.

51
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,240
She fought with heart like us.

52
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,794
I guess that's why she was so powerful.

53
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,017
You're right about that.

54
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:46,453
It's all a matter of perspective
when you think about it.

55
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:50,287
The knights see themselves as
good while you see them as evil.

56
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:53,425
But the reality is, you,
me, and these knights,

57
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:56,575
we're all human at the end of the day.

58
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,180
So who's to say who's good and who's bad?

59
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:01,600
Crap, almost forgot.

60
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:06,617
Could you give those two knuckleheads
some of that antidote for me?

61
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:09,397
Don't forget to snap their
daggers before you do.

62
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:12,715
Oh, and make sure they're
not packing any other tricks.

63
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:15,360
What about Administrator Kirito?

64
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:19,700
Will you be as understanding
of her as you are her knights?

65
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,740
System call!

66
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:36,669
Generate luminous element!

67
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:42,820
What's wrong?

68
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:46,680
I can't stop the bleeding.
Help me! Alright.

69
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,440
This isn't working.

70
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:54,585
She's lost way too much blood.

71
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:58,740
But I can't just let her die like this.

72
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:03,360
She's lived a hundred years
worrying, loving, suffering.

73
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,120
She was alive.

74
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:07,300
I can't let her soul get erased.

75
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,500
Help us.

76
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,738
This night's dying.

77
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:13,180
I know there's more of
you out there. Come on.

78
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,634
One of you needs help.

79
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,700
Can anyone hear me?

80
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:19,160
A priest, a monk, anyone?

81
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:21,580
She's dying.

82
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,537
Help her. Please.

83
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:24,940
You can't let her die.

84
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,050
That's it.

85
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,917
What do you think you're doing?

86
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,647
You're supposed to use
that on Administrator!

87
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:35,930
Yeah, I know!

88
00:06:36,013 --> 00:06:38,134
But if I use it on her, I can save her.

89
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:40,407
This tagger's her only hope.

90
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:41,920
I can save her with it!

91
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,660
I have to use it!

92
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:59,940
Goodness gracious, you
really are something!

93
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:02,557
Cardinal, she needs help.

94
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:05,337
I'm sorry, I know I shouldn't have.

95
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:08,479
I know what's happened, and
please, don't apologize.

96
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:12,477
I will heal Fanatio Synthesis 2. However,

97
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:15,277
I will have to bring her to me as it will

98
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:17,637
take some time to
initiate a full recovery.

99
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:24,137
These potions

100
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,557
will heal you now.

101
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:29,837
As far as I can tell, administrator
is not yet in her waking state.

102
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:33,357
If you can make it to the
top floor before she wakes,

103
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:36,637
you can still eliminate her
without the use of the dagger.

104
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,037
Hurry!

105
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,100
Only a few

106
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:42,617
integrity knights remain.

107
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,137
I kind of lost it there, sorry.

108
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:47,396
No, you don't ever have to apologize.

109
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,860
Hey, did you get that?

110
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,317
Cardinal said something weird just now.

111
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:03,460
Something about
Administrator's waking state.

112
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:06,607
Perhaps she spends most
of her time sleeping.

113
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:10,537
Cardinal said administrator
and some of her

114
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:13,097
knights have been around
for a couple of centuries.

115
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:15,497
So who knows what kind
of strain that puts on

116
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:18,737
him maybe it's part of
the deal administrator

117
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:24,180
Has to sleep all day to stay alive well i
guess we'll find out once we get up there.

118
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,700
What the heck is this?

119
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:52,260
Watch out!

120
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,558
Something's coming!

121
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:18,180
Thank you for waiting.

122
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,778
Which floor would you like to visit?

123
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,300
Which floor?

124
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:26,380
Do you mean you can take us
to any of the floors above?

125
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:35,120
Um, we're fugitives, and we sort
of like broke into the cathedral.

126
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:40,000
Isn't your Elevate, I mean, floating
thing off-limits to folks like us?

127
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:41,888
I'm not sure what you mean.

128
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:45,182
Anyone who wishes to use
this platform may do so.

129
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:48,100
My job is to merely
operate it, nothing more.

130
00:09:48,780 --> 00:09:49,610
Okay.

131
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:52,275
We'll take you up on your offer, then.

132
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:53,960
Hey, wait!

133
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,040
Are you sure it's safe?

134
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,660
Of course.

135
00:09:58,040 --> 00:10:00,177
Besides, there's no more stairs to climb.

136
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,497
Yeah, but...

137
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:02,597
Never mind.

138
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:06,680
All right, please take
us up as high as you can.

139
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,180
Right away, sir.

140
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,037
System call.

141
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,900
Generate aerial element.

142
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:20,960
Burst element.

143
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:34,662
So, uh, have you been
doing this for a while now?

144
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,440
As a matter of fact, I have.

145
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,240
For 107 years, actually.

146
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,100
107 years?

147
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:48,240
And this is all you do day in and
day out? Not quite. I get breaks.

148
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:51,757
I'm allowed to take one
at noon to have my lunch.

149
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:54,900
And then at night, I get
to sleep, so there's that.

150
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,120
That's not quite what I mean.

151
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,440
Um, what's your name?

152
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:01,100
My name.

153
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:04,160
I seem to have forgotten it.

154
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,260
That makes sense.

155
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:09,200
Operator is all anyone calls me anymore.

156
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,937
I think we can help.

157
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:18,240
We, um, we came here to bring
down the head of the church,

158
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:21,232
the one who forced this calling onto you.

159
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:22,660
You don't say.

160
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:27,017
If the church is gone, you'll
be released from your calling.

161
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,394
You'll be free to do whatever you want.

162
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,620
Is that so?

163
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,120
I'm at a loss.

164
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:37,656
I don't know anything of the
world outside this shaft.

165
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:41,960
Therefore, I have no idea what
new calling I would choose.

166
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:48,620
Although, if I could wish
for anything else to do...

167
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:58,020
I wish I could fly this platform
outside and go wherever I wanted.

168
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,720
Thank you for your patience.

169
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:13,400
This is the 80th floor,
the Cloudtop Garden.

170
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:18,757
I didn't think anything in this world
could be more boring than my calling,

171
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,940
but it's nothing compared to hers.

172
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:24,822
I could look forward to
growing old and retiring.

173
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,560
She's stuck with hers forever.

174
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:32,577
Cardinal said that even if you stopped
a person from aging with the sacred art,

175
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:35,307
there's no way to stop
their soul from aging.

176
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:39,820
Little by little, their memory crumbles,
and in the end, it falls apart.

177
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,860
The Axiom Church is straight-up evil.

178
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:50,117
We're the only ones who can stop
Administrator and free everyone.

179
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,030
It's a start.

180
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:55,097
But that's not the end
of this world's problems.

181
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:57,500
The real challenge is what comes after.

182
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:03,084
I thought after we defeated Administrator,
Cardinal would make things right again.

183
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:04,610
Won't she?

184
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:07,610
Sort of.

185
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:11,380
We can talk about it after
we get Alice back. Okay.

186
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:34,160
Oh, amazing.

187
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:05,910
Alice!

188
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:10,520
Please wait.

189
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:13,120
I want to let her soak in the sun.

190
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,180
Not for long.

191
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:17,240
A few more moments will do.

192
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,620
Let me do the fighting, okay?

193
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:25,540
Be ready with the dagger.

194
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:28,937
That's the only way
you're gonna get her back.

195
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:32,740
I'll block her strikes with my
body if it comes down to it.

196
00:14:33,860 --> 00:14:34,937
But can't we...

197
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,608
Look, there's no other way.

198
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,697
I'll charge Alice, take
the hit and pin her down.

199
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:42,380
Then you stick her with
the dagger. Got it?

200
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,150
Sorry.

201
00:14:44,233 --> 00:14:45,549
Nah, don't worry about it.

202
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:48,092
If this works, you can pay me back later.

203
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,629
I can't tell if she's
got her sword or not.

204
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,020
It doesn't matter.

205
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,597
We'll get to her before she can finish
casting her perfect weapon control.

206
00:14:56,680 --> 00:15:01,621
But we gotta attack now, because the more
we wait, the more time she has to cast it.

207
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:02,890
You're right.

208
00:15:02,973 --> 00:15:04,740
And if she does finish casting it,

209
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:08,757
I think I can use mine two more
times before I have to restore it.

210
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,428
And that's our backup plan.

211
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,737
I can only use mine one more time.

212
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:16,996
And we still got to deal with the
commander of the knights after Alice.

213
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:18,940
Come on, let's do this.

214
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:25,060
Against all odds, you two have
made it all the way up here.

215
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:28,780
I anticipated your escape from the prison.

216
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:31,800
But I did not anticipate
what happened next.

217
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:33,677
Eldrie should have caught you.

218
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,100
Yet you defeated him.

219
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,360
Then Deo Selbert.

220
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:37,900
I have no idea how.

221
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:40,777
And then, you defeated Fanatio as well.

222
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:43,220
And now you have set foot here.

223
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:44,760
It is shocking.

224
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:48,259
Where do you get the power
to overcome such knights?

225
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,951
Why do you wish to disrupt the order here?

226
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,518
Explain yourselves.

227
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,160
Very well.

228
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,580
I will get answers with my blade.

229
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,740
No way.

230
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,640
Damn it! Her sword!

231
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:13,640
It's already in perfect control.

232
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:47,640
Why did you not draw your swords?

233
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,080
If you were mocking me, know this.

234
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:54,240
I intentionally held back on that
strike just now as a warning.

235
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:57,480
The next one shall eliminate
your lives entirely.

236
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:03,280
For the honor of the knights you've
defeated, I insist you attack me in earnest.

237
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:08,380
System call.

238
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,197
Please accept our humble apologies.

239
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,940
We didn't mean to disrespect you just now.

240
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,760
My name is Kirito.

241
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:22,320
I'm a swordsman in training, and I
wish to duel with you, Lady Alice.

242
00:17:24,940 --> 00:17:25,770
Very well.

243
00:17:25,853 --> 00:17:30,380
Let us see just how wicked you are,
by the quality of your swordsmanship.

244
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:44,760
Before we start this up,
I got a question for you.

245
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:49,313
If that tree we saw just now is your
sword, that means it's its true form.

246
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:52,760
So how can a tree that
small be so powerful?

247
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:59,384
Long ago, the spot where the central
cathedral stands was the Place of Beginnings,

248
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:02,980
a place which Stacia,
the goddess of creation,

249
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,460
gifted to humanity.

250
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:09,000
In the center of a tiny village,
there was a beautiful spring.

251
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:13,200
On its banks, there grew
a single osmanthus tree.

252
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:17,940
This weapon, the osmanthus
blade, was forged from it.

253
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:22,260
A tree created by the
goddess reincarnated.

254
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:26,800
The oldest thing in existence,
a divine weapon indeed.

255
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:30,317
Everlasting eternity is its attribute.

256
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:35,200
A single petal can split stone
or tear the ground asunder.

257
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:37,560
You don't say.

258
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:39,035
That's a great score.

259
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:41,966
It's this world's first
indestructible object.

